projects.description:
Strengthening capacity of potato farms to achieve high yields of good quality potatoes.

Productive potential of the potato sector increased via:
- technical support provided to national potato cultivar registration and seed potato certification;
- capacity building support provided to researchers in the area of modernization of potato sector;
- capacity building support provided on on-farm practices for the production of high-quality seed potatoes and ware potatoes.

Regional project focusing on:
- Innovative practices and technologies to sustainably increase productivity, address climate change and environmental degradation;
- Capacities on market-based institutional arrangements supportive of inclusive and efficient agri-food systems.

Sustainable development of small ruminants production in the SEC region focusing on:
- Innovative practices and technologies to sustainably increase productivity, address climate change and environmental degradation;
- Capacities on cross-sectoral policy dialogue for integrated policies on sustainable agriculture, forestry and fisheries, address climate change and environmental degradation).

Global project focusing on:
- Policy and institutional capacity of government institutions; 
- Agri-food value chains and access to markets; 
- Sustainable productivity while addressing climate change and environmental degradation; 
- Access of the rural poor to productive resources, services and markets.

- Development of inclusive education conceptual framework, standards/requirements and mechanisms for inclusive and protective preschools and schools;
- Modelling of inclusive pre-schools and schools through the piltoing and operationalization of the standards/requirements and mechanisms developed as part of the conceptual framework and policy for inclusive education;
- Designing of C4D campaign for promoting Inclusive Education, and for eliminating stigma and discrimination, including abuse and violence, against children with disabilities;
- Undertake pre-service and in-service teachers' training to align with new competency-based curriculum and introduce new courses on teaching SEN children
- Exchange of best practices in development and implementation of policies and preschool and school-based practices on Inclusive Education;

Enhanced accessibility and availability of food through environmentally safe and economically viable aquaculture management applications. focusing on:
- Accessibility and availability of food through efficient & environmentally safe aquaculture management; 
- Capacities on cross-sectoral policies to eradicate hunger, food insecurity and malnutrition; 
- Capacities on integrated practices to increase productivity and production, address climate change; 
- Integration of agriculture, forestry and fisheries in international governance mechanisms;  
- Policies on rural poor's access to & control over services, finance, knowledge, technologies, markets and natural resources; 
- Standards for food safety and quality & plant health).

Regional project focusing on:
-  Capacities to collect, analyze and report data for decision-making on sustainable production, climate change and environmental degradation;
- Mechanisms to identify, monitor threats, and assess risks and deliver integrated and timely Early Warning; 
- Capacities on prevention and mitigation good practices to reduce impacts of threats and crises).
